"""Local comparison for the Parisian facade correction; no publication/upload."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,base64,html
out=Path('build/resort-blocks/paris')
def img(p,label):
 p=Path(p);mime='image/jpeg' if p.suffix=='.jpg' else 'image/png'
 return '<figure><figcaption>'+html.escape(label)+'</figcaption><img loading="lazy" src="data:'+mime+';base64,'+base64.b64encode(p.read_bytes()).decode()+'"></figure>'
rows=[('tools/resort-blocks/references/paris-entrance-earth-2026-10-05.png','REFERENCE · Creator Google Earth aerial; acquisition date unknown'),(out/'game-facades-aerial.jpg','GAME · Final facade correction in the installed game'),(out/'facades-before-aerial.png','BEFORE · Previous facade geometry, neutral-light review'),(out/'facades-aerial-review.png','AFTER · Exported facade geometry, same neutral review camera'),(out/'facades-review.png','DETAIL · French windows, shutters, balcony scrollwork, awnings and dormers'),(out/'game-facades.jpg','GAME · Close review from above the motor court')]
validation=json.loads((out/'facade-validation.json').read_text())
page='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Parisian arrival facades · 2026-10-05</title><style>body{margin:32px;background:#182124;color:#edf1ed;font:17px/1.5 system-ui}h1{font-size:32px}p{max-width:1100px}main{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}figure{margin:0}figcaption{margin:10px 0;color:#b2d9d1}img{width:100%}a{color:#b2d9d1}pre{white-space:pre-wrap}li{margin:8px 0}@media(max-width:850px){main{display:block}figure{margin-bottom:24px}}</style><h1>Paris · Parisian facades around the Arc</h1><p>The curved arrival frontage now reads as adjoining French facades: paired narrow windows, projecting sills, scroll iron balconies, selected shutters, red awnings, alternate pediments and dormers, subtly stepped slate roofs and chimney pots. The right-hand pavilion now also has its courtyard-facing return.</p><p>The footprint, working entrance and curb ramp are retained. Static details use shared materials and 64-metre cells; no per-window colliders or lights. Wider texture-atlas gutters with replicated corners remove the bright repeat seams seen on the reviewed dark roofs.</p><main>'''+''.join(img(*r) for r in rows)+'''</main><h2>Reference register</h2><p>The creator aerial is the primary composition reference. <a href="https://www.cs.kent.edu/~walker/photos/01-06-15lasvegas.html">Robert A. Walker's June 2001 photo set</a>, <a href="https://www.cs.kent.edu/~walker/photos/01-06-15_LasVegas/Images/photo119.jpg">arrival photograph</a>, corroborates the Parisian bay/roof/awning character. It is historical evidence, not a current signage survey. <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/davetoussaint/4851433594">Dave Toussaint's 2010 entrance photo</a> is recorded for future coffered-vault lobby work. Reference pixels were not imported as game textures.</p><h2>Limits and unfinished work</h2><p>Dimensions, individual window counts, chimney positions and ornament are fitted interpretations. The present vestibule is not a reconstruction of the photographed vaulted hall. Fine reliefs, mature landscaping, service elevations and the rest of the full-block acceptance checklist remain in paris.json. Camera directions are useful for comparison but not photogrammetrically calibrated. Paris remains active; this does not mark the resort complete.</p><h2>Validation</h2><pre>'''+html.escape(json.dumps(validation,indent=2))+'''</pre>'''
(out/'facade-proof.html').write_text(page);print(out/'facade-proof.html')
